#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""vibekeyd: Ulanzi Vibekey (AU05) control-surface daemon for Manjaro KDE (X11) — vibekey port.

Ported from jimmibram/vibekey-driver (MIT, upstream @ 41ba904b); buildable
spec: spec.md at the repo root. What it does
  * Finds the Dongle (USB fff1:00dd) and holds both of its raw HID channels
    open. The Dongle's watchdog re-enumerates it; holding the channels is the
    cure — presses in a reboot window vanish, which is normal.
  * Reads the standard HID reports straight from hidraw, so the Voice Control
    is seen too: from the factory it sends the HID "ErrorRollOver" usage
    (0x01), which the kernel never turns into a key press. Other firmware
    sends Super+H instead.
  * EVIOCGRABs the device's evdev nodes so factory keystrokes never reach
    X11/libinput — every one except the mouse-named node, whose wheel reports
    pass through while the Knob mode is `scroll` (spec §2). Every Control runs
    its Assignment from ~/.config/vibekey/config.json instead.
  * Key combos fire as `xdotool key` (one-shot); Dictation brackets the chord
    with `xdotool keydown/keyup` against handy's Tauri backend (spec §2.2).
  * Behaviors (spec §5): dictation.ptt, session.next/prev/focus/interrupt,
    orca.worktree.next/prev, sessions.turn — Daemon-side Presets.
  * Owns the device's indicator lights through a single-writer lighting module
    (TEA-encrypted vendor frames on interface 3; spec §5.5), including the
    Device lighting mode policy (guest + consented Manage lights).
  * Polls the battery and publishes everything the Panel needs to
    $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/vibekey/state.json.

Only the Python standard library is used.

Usage: vibekeyd [--probe] [--no-grab] [--no-battery] [--no-lighting]
  --probe        also print every decoded control event to stdout
  --no-grab      leave the evdev nodes alone (keystrokes reach apps as well)
  --no-battery   never talk to the vendor channel
  --no-lighting  skip all lighting traffic (device-mode policy, ring, blinks)
"""

